    <string name="setup_orientation_title">IMU orientation</string>
    <string name="setup_orientation_body">Pick how the board sits in the machine: which face points up, then what points forward. The app writes both orientation fields from that choice: the axis roles (which chip axis is up, which measures the pitch rate) and the six signs. Every pose is a proper rotation; the board refuses any other frame at boot and does not bring up its IMU.</string>
    <string name="setup_orientation_family">The poses assume the standard board family\'s chip mount (the measured yaw, not the firmware\'s compiled fallback). A board of another family needs its chip mount measured before these poses are right for it.</string>
    <!-- %1$s is the six signs, e.g. [-1, 1, -1, -1, 1, -1]. -->
    <string name="setup_orientation_stored">Stored map: %1$s</string>
    <string name="setup_orientation_stored_unread">Stored map: not read</string>
    <!-- %1$s is the chip axis playing UP, %2$s the one playing PITCH_RATE, e.g. Z and Y. -->
    <string name="setup_orientation_roles">Stored roles: UP = %1$s, PITCH_RATE = %2$s</string>
    <string name="setup_orientation_roles_unread">Stored roles: not read</string>
    <!-- %1$s is a pose name (setup_pose_name) or a custom frame (setup_pose_custom). -->
    <string name="setup_orientation_runs">Runs as: %1$s</string>
    <string name="setup_orientation_stored_as">Stored as: %1$s. The board runs the stored map from its next power-up, not now.</string>
    <string name="setup_orientation_unset">Unset signs and roles run the firmware fallback.</string>
    <string name="setup_orientation_mirrored">The stored frame is not a proper rotation (mirrored, or an invalid pair of roles). The board refuses it at boot and does not bring up its IMU. Pick a pose below before it is next powered up.</string>
